{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mass.WedderburnMassFormulaCoefficients","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mass.WedderburnMassFormulaCoefficients","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.QIntegerCanonical"],"declarations":4,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.WedderburnMassFormulaCoefficients.coeffs_inconsistent_of_ne","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.WedderburnMassFormulaCoefficients.coeffs_inconsistent_of_ne","kind":"theorem","line":90,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/WedderburnMassFormulaCoefficients.lean#L90-L98","doc":"**The contrapositive, as the audit actually uses it.** A recorded pair\nfailing `2·β₃ + β₂ + 6 = 0` cannot be the published formula's two coefficients —\nfor **any** `q`.  This is what makes the finding independent of which pin, which\nconvention, and which rounding produced the recorded numbers. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.WedderburnMassFormulaCoefficients.beta3_of_beta2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.WedderburnMassFormulaCoefficients.beta3_of_beta2","kind":"theorem","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/WedderburnMassFormulaCoefficients.lean#L69-L88","doc":"**The dependency.** Given the published shapes `β₂ = −2[3]_q` and\n`β₃ = h_A²`, the two coefficients satisfy one linear relation with **no `q` in\nit at all**:\n\n    2·β₃ + β₂ + 6 = 0        (equivalently `β₃ = −β₂/2 − 3` wherever `2` is a unit)\n\nSo the correction term carries **one** q-integer degree of freedom, not two.\nStated multiplicatively to stay valid in every characteristic — dividing by `2`\nwould need `(2 : R) ≠ 0`, a hypothesis the content does not require.\n\nFalsifiable, and it is exactly what the recorded pair `(β₂, β₃) =\n(−6.087415, 0.0499)` violates: it evaluates to `2(0.0499) − 6.087415 + 6 =\n+0.012385`, not `0`.  The same `β₂` forces `β₃ = 0.0437073`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.WedderburnMassFormulaCoefficients.haSq_eq_qIntBal_three_sub_three","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.WedderburnMassFormulaCoefficients.haSq_eq_qIntBal_three_sub_three","kind":"theorem","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/WedderburnMassFormulaCoefficients.lean#L58-L67","doc":"**The identity.** The Hecke–Skein parameter squared is the third balanced\nq-integer, shifted by `3`:  `h_A² = [3]_q − 3`.\n\nNeeds `q ≠ q⁻¹` only because `qIntBal` divides by `q − q⁻¹`; at `q = ±1` the\nquantum integer degenerates and the statement is vacuous rather than false. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.WedderburnMassFormulaCoefficients.qIntBal_three_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.WedderburnMassFormulaCoefficients.qIntBal_three_eq","kind":"theorem","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/WedderburnMassFormulaCoefficients.lean#L51-L56","doc":"**The third balanced q-integer, in closed form**: `[3]_q = q² + 1 + q⁻²`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}